1
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:36,000
When it comes to family and relationships, there are no small surprises.

2
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Gigantic is a comedy, romance film directed by Matt Aselton.

3
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:36,000
Young mattress salesman Brian decides to adopt a baby from China but is distracted when he forms
a relationship with quirky, wealthy Harriet whom he meets at his mattress store.

4
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:06,000
As their relationship flourishes, unbeknownst to
them, a hitman is trying to kill Brian.

5
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:36,000
Happy, played by Zooey Deschanel.

6
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Happy's Father, played by John Goodman.

7
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:36,000
Brian, played by Paul Dano.

8
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Kirby Weathersby, played by Ed Asner.

9
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Barbara Weathersby, played by Jane Alexander.

10
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
John Weathersby, played by Ian Roberts.

11
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
Gigantic is a 2008 independent comedy film directed by Matt Aselton and starring Paul
Dano, Zooey Deschanel, John Goodman, Edward Asner and Jane Alexander.

12
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
The script, written by Aselton and his college friend Adam Nagata, tells of Brian (Dano), a mattress salesman who wishes to adopt a baby
from China, but finds himself sharing his passion with the quirky, wealthy Harriet (Deschanel) when they meet in his store.

13
01:11:30,000 --> 01:11:36,000
The story was based on Aselton's childhood wish for
his parents to adopt a Chinese baby.

14
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
The film was shot in New York and Connecticut.

15
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
It had its world premiere at 2008's Toronto International Film Festival
and was released in the United States on April 3, 2009.

16
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
The film explores themes of department store,
adoption, chinese woman, stalker, stalking.

17
01:33:30,000 --> 01:33:36,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
